      body:`<p>Measure each day's move in <b>standard deviations</b> (sd): the size of a typical day. A <b>standard deviation</b> (sd) is the usual size of a day's move. A 4-sd day moves four times as much as usual. (replaces the whole first sentence)</p>
            <p>If daily moves followed a <b>bell curve</b> (a "normal distribution"), days that big would almost never come. The S&amp;P 500 has had dozens.</p>`,
function cards() {
  const c = M.crash_years;
